course: dictionary
lesson: 6000
title: Meat and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Meat is the flesh of animals, such as cows, pigs, sheep and chickens, that people eat as food. «They gave milk, wool, meat, eggs and muscle power, and let people settle in villages.» Here meat is one of the things farm animals gave people.
explain: Meat is a noun you cannot count. You say some meat, not two meat. You can say meats when you mean different kinds, such as beef and lamb. Check the sentence to see which one fits.
explain: Context helps you here. «Some people eat meat; vegetarians and vegans do not.» The sentence sets meat against vegetarians, so meat must be a food. Vegetarians do not eat meat, and vegans eat no animal foods at all.
fact: Meat is the flesh of animals, such as cows, pigs, sheep and chickens, eaten as food.
fact: Meat gives us protein, which helps build muscles, so a balanced diet can include meat, fish, beans and eggs.
fact: Animals that eat mainly meat are called carnivores.
fact: Raw meat can carry germs, so keep it away from other food, wash your hands and chopping boards after touching it, and cook it all the way through with no pink.
fact: «Spam» is also a brand of tinned meat, as well as the word for junk messages.
exercise: «They gave milk, wool, meat, eggs and muscle power, and let people settle in villages.» Which word in this sentence is the flesh of animals eaten as food? | villages | wool | muscle power | *meat
exercise: A carnivore is an animal that eats mainly what? | Milk | Plants | Sand | *Meat
exercise: Why should you wash the chopping board after touching raw meat? | Because meat is made of wool | *Raw meat can carry germs | To keep the board warm | To make the meat go pink
test: «Some people eat meat; vegetarians and vegans do not.» Which group eats no animal foods at all, not even milk or eggs? | *Vegans | Carnivores | Vegetarians | Marsupials
test: Raw chicken should be cooked how, to keep you safe? | Served raw with sauce | Left out overnight to cool | *All the way through, with no pink in it | Just warmed on the outside
exam: «The thylacine, or Tasmanian tiger, was a striped meat-eating marsupial.» What does meat-eating tell you about the thylacine? | It lived in the sea | It ate only plants and fruit | *It ate the flesh of other animals | It had no stripes
